WEBVTT

00:02:29.097 --> 00:02:30.108
(Laughter)

00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:32.336
So I don't really know that,
I don't really --

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.832
actually, I do my own kind
of research, you know?

00:02:34.856 --> 00:02:38.337
If I'm commissioned to do the costumes
for an 18th-century opera

00:02:38.361 --> 00:02:39.763
or something like that,

00:02:39.787 --> 00:02:42.395
I will do a lot of research,
because it's interesting,

00:02:42.419 --> 00:02:45.236
not because it's what I'm supposed to do.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.976
I'm very, very, very inspired by movies.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.976
The color of movies
and the way light makes the colors.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.284
Light from behind the projection
or light from the projection

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.976
makes the colors look so impossible.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.885
Anyway, roll this little clip.
I'll just show you.